    "media:imagetext": "AR TRANSPOR\nPAA\nIN REPLY REFE\nTO NO.\nUNITED STATES FLEET\nNAVAL AIR TRANSPORT SERVICE COMMAND\nU.S. NAVAL AUXILIARY AIR STATION\nOAKLAND. 14. CALIFORNIA\nJuly 15, 1945.\nEMPLOYEES OF PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS:\nYou who have been flying and maintaining Naval Air\nTransport Service Planes in many parts of the world,\nand you\nwho have remained at outlying bases helping to keep the Navy's\nfar flung air transport system in operation, have made a vital\ncontribution toward final victory.\nThis work has involved\nserious supply problems, and the service you men and women have\nnone to a son er the sting one ban of the breast.\nPlease accept my congratulations on a job well done.\nW.\nReuros\nRear Admiral J. W. Reeves, Jr., USN\nComnander, Naval Air Transport Service\nTITLE\nStudent Pilot\nJunior Pilot\nJunior Pilot\nRecord of Service\nJOHN\n3.\nRUSSELL\nL O\nCATION\nSan Francisco\nSan Francisco\nContract terminated\nDATES\n1-7-43\n5-2-43\n11-15-45\n201\n1026",
